@startuml metadata_runtime_directory_mapping
title Managed Metadata to CampusClaw Runtime Directory
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 30

' Source evidence (CampusClaw PR 167 f60cc3e78bb8b700527ac082c7c8e10524ede095):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java, prepare and materialize.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/agent/FileAgentDirectoryResolver.java, resolve.
' Observed behavior: the Java baseline has two file contracts and materializes the legacy CLI tree in place.
' Architecture change: one managed tree serves Runtime, Cron, and Subagent entry points.
' Security hardening: a complete sibling tree is validated before publication.
' Design reason: sessions consume immutable identity indexes and never persist remote tool lists.
' Architecture change: refresh publishes metadata only; the next idle execution reconciles its model.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam file {
  BackgroundColor #F0FDF4
  BorderColor #16A34A
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

rectangle "Mate runtime snapshot" as Input {
  rectangle "Current Agent identity\nand model bindings" as AgentMetadata
  rectangle "Direct Skill identities\nand package resources" as SkillMetadata
  rectangle "Direct Subagent identities\nand fixed versions" as SubagentMetadata
}

rectangle "AgentRuntimeManager" as Manager {
  rectangle "prepare cache-first\nrefresh explicitly" as Resolve
  rectangle "Build sibling tree" as Build
  rectangle "Validate names, IDs,\nversions, files, and boundaries" as Validate
  rectangle "Publish complete tree" as Publish
}

rectangle "Managed Agent directory\nagent/{agentId}/.campusclaw/" as AgentDirectory {
  file "agent.json\ncurrent identity only" as AgentFile
  file "settings.json\ndefaultModel, bindingModels" as SettingsFile
  file "SYSTEM.md\nAgent instructions" as SystemFile
  file "agents/{agentName}.json\ndirect Subagent identity and version" as SubagentFile
  file "skills/{skillName}/skill.json\nSkill identity and version" as SkillIdentityFile
  file "skills/{skillName}/SKILL.md\nreferences, templates" as SkillPackage
}

database "Mate metadata authority\nAgent, Skill, Subagent bindings" as MateAuthority
database "Model Manager authority\nmodel availability and credentials" as ModelManager
rectangle "Execution preparation" as Execution {
  rectangle "Immutable name indexes" as Indexes
  rectangle "AgentSessionFactory" as SessionFactory
  rectangle "Next-execution model reconciler" as Reconciler
  database "Runtime Session store" as SessionStore
  rectangle "Active execution snapshot" as ActiveSnapshot
}

AgentMetadata --> Resolve
SkillMetadata --> Resolve
SubagentMetadata --> Resolve
Resolve --> Build
Build --> Validate
Validate --> Publish
Publish --> AgentDirectory

Resolve .right.> MateAuthority : cold prepare / refresh
SettingsFile .right.> ModelManager : bound models
AgentDirectory -down-> Indexes : scan exact names
Indexes --> SessionFactory : Skill and direct Subagent resolution
AgentDirectory -down-> SessionFactory : prompt, workspace,\nmodel settings
AgentDirectory -down-> Reconciler : next idle execution
SessionStore --> Reconciler : current model and thinking
Reconciler --> SessionStore : optional atomic model/thinking\nchange entries before User Entry
AgentDirectory .down.> ActiveSnapshot : freeze for execution
ActiveSnapshot -[hidden]right-> SessionStore

note right of AgentDirectory
No remote tool list is written to disk.
The tree is read-only between publications.
Name and path must match byte-for-byte.
Refresh does not mutate active snapshots.
end note

note left of Manager
Complete cache hits do not call Mate.
Refresh failure keeps the old directory.
No TTL or version-driven auto refresh.
end note

note bottom of Reconciler
Keep the current model while it remains callable.
Otherwise select the usable new default.
Reject before accepting a User Entry if none exists.
end note
AgentFile -[hidden]down-> SubagentFile
SettingsFile -[hidden]down-> SkillIdentityFile
SystemFile -[hidden]down-> SkillPackage
AgentDirectory -[hidden]down-> Execution
MateAuthority -[hidden]down-> ModelManager
@enduml
